      "math_academy_id": "q-15939",
      "sequence_position": 4,
      "problem": "Find the average rate of change of the function $f(x)$ on the interval $[-3,1]$ given the following table of values for $f(x):$\n\n| $x$ | $\\,-3\\,$ | $\\,-2\\,$ | $\\,-1\\,$ | $\\,0\\,$ | $\\,1\\,$ | $\\,2\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\,2\\,$ | $\\,-2\\,$ | $\\,1\\,$ | $\\,2\\,$ | $\\,-3\\,$ | $\\,-3\\,$ |",
      "worked_solution": "Using the formula for the averge rate of change, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{Δf}{Δx} & =\\frac{f(b)-f(a)}{b-a} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(1)-f(-3)}{1-(-3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-3-2}{1-(-3)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
